# Third Party — PHP 8.5 Upgrade Rules

Libraries in `app/third_party/` and `app/libraries/razorpay/`.

## Subagent First

Use `explore` subagent to list all references to the library in `app/` before upgrading. Use `shell` subagent to run PHP lint/test after swap.

## Upgrade Map (behavior must stay same)

| Library | Action | Used By |
|---------|--------|---------|
| MPDF | Upgrade to 8.x | PDF bills, challans, reports |
| PHPExcel | Migrate to PhpSpreadsheet | CSV/Excel import-export |
| Stripe (old) | New Stripe SDK | POS, Webshop payments |
| PayPal | Update SDK | Payment gateways |
| phpqrcode | Compat check only | Barcodes, QR |
| Google/Facebook SDK | Update or trim to OAuth only | Social login |

## Rules

- Replace library calls with equivalent API — **same file output, same data format**.
- Do not vendor entire new ecosystems; trim unused Google API services if possible.
- `(integer)`/`(boolean)` casts in PHPExcel/MPDF — fix during migration, not in app code.
- Test PDF generation and Excel import/export after each lib upgrade.
- Keep `app/third_party/` paths working — update autoload/includes, not consumer logic.

## Do Not

- Rewrite app controllers to use new patterns when a drop-in lib swap works.
- Delete `third_party` folders without verifying zero references in `app/`.
